<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of David</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Davidic line</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> was the dynasty that, according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>, descended from King David and ruled the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> for about four centuries, until the Babylonian conquest of 587/586 BCE. The phrase appears in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tel-dan-stele">Tel Dan stele</a> of the 9th century BCE, its earliest known mention outside the Bible. Jewish and Christian tradition expected the Messiah to come from David's line.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-david.jpg" alt="House of David" width="320" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Star_of_David.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
